Explicit VA-API encoding GPU and opt-in cross-device staging.

LOWLAT_VAAPI_DEVICE selects an encoder render node independently from the
captured output. Different devices use explicit eight-bit NV12 RAM staging;
the default keeps its original GPU handle path. Prefer cached readback memory
to avoid slow CPU reads from uncached GPU BAR memory.

Tested RTX 5070 DP-1 capture -> RX 570 H.264/HEVC encoding. Both streams
decode through FFmpeg. This adds latency and does not promise 144 FPS.

